{"parentUuid":"b8e24c92-b00f-4cd4-a986-1e8bb120a3d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01QWjRUFEzV61ubvonc33ZpN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TgDxKhvmMKadDmmaFb9aAr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nfix(migrate): sync from origin so stale local refs don't hide v2 gaps\n\n`entire migrate --checkpoints v2` previously walked LOCAL v1 (which the\ndefault fetch refspec never updates) and used LOCAL v2/main for the\n\"already migrated\" check. Two failure modes followed:\n\n- Checkpoints created on other clones were invisible to migrate until\n  local v1 was manually pulled — they live on origin/entire/checkpoints/v1\n  but not on the local branch.\n- A v2 entry that existed in local v2 but never made it to origin (e.g.\n  a dual-write whose v2/main push got dropped in a merge race) was\n  forever skipped as \"already migrated\", leaving the entry permanently\n  missing on origin no matter how many times migrate ran.\n\nNow migrate fetches origin's v1 and v2/main into staging refs at startup,\nsafely fast-forwards the local refs (no-op when local is ahead or has\ndiverged), and uses origin's v2/main root tree for the existence check\nvia a new V2GitStore.ReadCommittedFromTree helper. When origin lacks an\nentry but local has one, the local copy is auto-pruned so the rewrite\nproduces a non-empty commit on /main that the next push delivers.\n\nFailures are non-fatal: missing origin refs (first migration on the repo,\noffline) fall back to the prior local-only behavior by passing\nplumbing.ZeroHash as the origin tree.\n\nTests cover the three new states — origin has but local doesn't (skip),\nlocal has but origin doesn't (re-emit, the regression test for the bug),\nand both agree (existing skip+backfill path).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -10","description":"Create commit"},"caller":{"type":"dire